.Dd April 19, 2026
.Dt CMI_KERNELSTORE 4
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm cmi_kernelstore
.Nd CMI shared key-value store
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Cd "kldload cmi"
.Cd "kldload cmi_kernelstore"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
service provides a shared, capability-gated key-value store.
The capability fd IS the credential \(em if you hold it, you can
read and write.
No UID check, no separate authentication.
.Pp
Connecting creates a new empty store.
The owner can mint member fds to share access with other processes.
All holders operate on the same backing store.
Closing the last fd destroys the store and all its data.
.Pp
Two roles exist:
.Bl -tag -width "Member"
.It Sy Owner
Can PUT, GET, DELETE, and MINT.
.It Sy Member
Can PUT, GET, and DELETE.
Cannot MINT further members.
.El
.Pp
To revoke a member's access, the owner calls
.Dv CMI_TERMINATE
on the member fd.
.Pp
All operations use
.Dv CMI_CALL
(synchronous).
.Ss Operations
.Bl -tag -width KSTORE_OP_DELETE
.It Dv KSTORE_OP_PUT
Store a value under a string key.
The value follows the request struct in the payload.
Overwrites existing keys.
.It Dv KSTORE_OP_GET
Retrieve a value by key.
Returns
.Dv KSTORE_STATUS_NOTFOUND
if the key does not exist.
Returns
.Er EMSGSIZE
if the reply buffer is too small.
.It Dv KSTORE_OP_DELETE
Remove a key.
.It Dv KSTORE_OP_MINT
Create a member fd (owner only).
Returned as a reply fd.
.El
.Ss Limits
.Bl -tag -width KSTORE_MAX_VALUE
.It Dv KSTORE_MAX_KEYS
256 keys per store.
.It Dv KSTORE_MAX_VALUE
4096 bytes per value.
.It Dv KSTORE_KEY_MAX
64 bytes per key name.
.El
.Ss Wire protocol
.Bd -literal
#include <cmi_kernelstore_proto.h>

struct kstore_request {
    uint32_t op;
    uint32_t _reserved;
    char     key[KSTORE_KEY_MAX];
};

struct kstore_status_reply {
    uint32_t status;
};
.Ed
.Pp
PUT appends the value after the
.Vt kstore_request
in the request payload.
GET returns the value after the
.Vt kstore_status_reply
in the reply payload.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr cmi 4
